  "notes": [
    "10BASE-T transmitter (docs/extension-study.md section 7.1): TD+ on pin 0, TD- on pin 1 (the pair pin, PINS clock field). Manchester at P = 2: 50 ns half-bits at a 40 MHz clock (4 cycles per bit).",
    "When the TX queue has data it sends the preamble and SFD (made on chip) and then 17 queue words (COUNT 16: a 68-byte frame from destination address to FCS, LSB first), with no gap between words; then TP_IDL (positive for 12 cycles, 300 ns) and silence.",
    "While the TX queue is empty it sends a 100 ns link pulse (NLP) every 640,000 cycles (16.0 ms at 40 MHz).",
    "The FCS comes from the host. Frames longer than the TX queue are staged through relay engines (relay.source.json).",
    "Needs the line unit (options.line_unit rec16, docs/extension.md); assemble with --variant configs/variants/diet8_rec16.json."
  ]
